# End-to-End DevOps Deployment Challenge

A 2-day capstone. No new lecture content today — this is where everything from Linux, Git, Docker, Terraform, Azure, Kubernetes, and Jenkins gets applied, independently, to an application of your own choosing.

## Organisation

### Duration

2 days, **09:30 - 17:00** each day. This is deliberately less structured than previous sessions — students work independently or in pairs, with trainers acting as **mentors and reviewers** rather than lecturing from the front.

| Day | Focus |
|---|---|
| Day 1 | Choose your application, containerise it, provision infrastructure, get it manually deployed |
| Day 2 | Automate the whole thing with Jenkins, harden it, and demo it to the group |

### Set-up

#### For Trainers

This session runs differently to the rest of the course — plan your day as a **facilitator**, not a lecturer.

- **Prepare** a short kickoff (15 min max) covering the brief, the checkpoints, and the support model — everything after that is roaming, reviewing, and unblocking
- **Schedule** yourself around the four checkpoints below so you're free to check in with each student/pair as they hit them, rather than at fixed lecture times
- **Prepare** a shared space (a channel, a whiteboard, a shared doc) for students to log where they're stuck — this makes it much easier to spot common blockers early and address them once to the whole room, rather than repeating the same fix one-to-one
- **Have example applications ready** (see below) for anyone who arrives without a project of their own
- **Book time** at the end of Day 2 for the showcase — this matters more than it might seem; presenting their own work is a big part of the learning here

**Optional Slidee slide** for the kickoff only: <br>
`Weeks X Y > CDO > End-to-End Deployment Challenge` — just the brief and checkpoint timings, nothing more.

#### For Students
- **Direct** students to the starter code for this module
  - [Student Facing Repo](https://github.com/LaFosseAcademy/cloud-devops-student-repos/tree/main)
- **Use**
  - **/end-to-end-challenge/starter-code** — contains the example applications below, plus a blank project template with a suggested folder structure (not mandatory to use)
- **Make sure** everyone has, before Day 1 starts:
  - A GitHub account and the ability to create a new repository
  - Docker installed and running
  - A Docker Hub account (or access to Azure Container Registry, if preferred)
  - An Azure subscription with a Service Principal ready to go (from the Terraform/Azure sessions)
  - A working Jenkins instance (their own from the Jenkins day, or a shared one provided by the trainer)
  - **Chosen an application** — see below

## Learning objectives

- **Apply** Linux, Git, Docker, Terraform, Azure, and Jenkins together on one real project, independently
- **Design and justify** your own architecture and toolchain decisions, rather than following a prescribed path
- **Produce** a working, automated deployment pipeline — from `git push` to a live, reachable application
- **Practice** troubleshooting across the full stack without step-by-step instructions
- **Present** and demonstrate a finished solution clearly to peers

